      "chief_complaint": "New confusion, worse than baseline",
      "hpi": "An 81-year-old woman with mild major neurocognitive disorder is admitted for two days of confusion that her caregiver says is worse than baseline. At baseline she recognizes family. Temperature is 37.9 C. Urinalysis shows leukocyte esterase, and the urine culture grows Escherichia coli. She finishes five days of nitrofurantoin 100 mg orally twice daily before discharge. Outpatient creatinine is 1.1 mg/dL, admission creatinine is 1.3 mg/dL, and discharge creatinine is 1.2 mg/dL. That small change is not treated as acute kidney injury. A pharmacy list confirms lisinopril 10 mg daily and atorvastatin 40 mg daily. Neither is stopped. There is no statin adverse effect on the chart. Confusion is back to the caregiver's baseline at discharge, and she is afebrile.",
